// =============================================================================
// Detection: Legacy authentication usage
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   Sign-ins using legacy / basic-auth protocols (POP, IMAP, SMTP AUTH, MAPI,
//   EWS, ActiveSync, Outlook Anywhere, Outlook Service, Reporting Web
//   Services, "Other clients"), interactive OR non-interactive. These
//   protocols cannot enforce MFA and are the classic bypass for Conditional
//   Access — they are the single most common foothold in password-spray
//   compromise. The lab blocks them with a CA policy; this rule proves the
//   block holds and surfaces anything still trying (an app or service account
//   that needs modernising).
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   union of:
//     SigninLogs                        (interactive user sign-ins)
//     AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs   (token refresh / background clients)
//   Both from Microsoft Entra ID -> Diagnostic settings -> Log Analytics.
//   Microsoft's "Identify legacy authentication use" steps say to repeat the
//   check on the User sign-ins (non-interactive) tab, so query both tables.
//   Identified via ClientAppUsed. Modern clients are "Browser" and "Mobile
//   Apps and Desktop clients"; the list below covers every legacy protocol
//   Microsoft documents for the CA Client apps condition (Exchange ActiveSync
//   + Other clients). The commented-out negative filter also catches labels
//   Microsoft adds later.
//
// LICENSE
//   - SigninLogs + AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs export requires Entra ID P1.
//   - Blocking legacy auth via Conditional Access requires Entra ID P1.
//   - Runs as a Log Analytics scheduled query or a Microsoft Sentinel rule.
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Service accounts / multifunction printers / old line-of-business apps
//     often still speak SMTP AUTH or EWS; expect a short allow-list during
//     migration, tracked to an owner and an end date — not permanently muted.
//   - A legacy attempt that FAILS (ResultType != "0") usually means CA already
//     blocked it — good news; the Successes count is where to focus.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   As deployed by lab/terraform/modules/monitoring: Frequency 1h · Lookback
//   24h · Trigger > 0 rows · suppressed 23 h after an alert · no entity
//   mapping (summarized output). Suggested tuning (not deployed): alert
//   hardest on Successes > 0.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE (Logic App - lab/monitoring/playbook-notify.json)
//   Shared by all five rules, Sentinel path only (the post-trial Log
//   Analytics alerts just email the ag-identity-secops action group).
//   Incident created -> automation rule (lab/terraform/modules/monitoring) ->
//   (1) Teams adaptive card: incident severity, title, number, created time,
//       status, description and an "Open in Sentinel" link;
//   (2) ServiceNow incident: urgency/impact from severity (Low -> 3),
//       category "inquiry"; (3) the INC number is commented back on the
//       Sentinel incident for the audit trail.
//   The incident is how the owning team is driven off basic auth.
// =============================================================================

// Explicit legacy-client list (clearest for the screen-share). verify: names
// against your tenant — Microsoft occasionally relabels ClientAppUsed values.
let LegacyClients = dynamic([
    "Exchange ActiveSync", "IMAP4", "IMAP", "POP3", "POP",
    "SMTP", "Authenticated SMTP", "MAPI", "MAPI Over HTTP",
    "Exchange Web Services", "Exchange Online PowerShell",
    "Outlook Anywhere (RPC over HTTP)", "Outlook Service", "AutoDiscover",
    "Offline Address Book", "Reporting Web Services", "Other clients"
]);
// Same two tables as break-glass-signin.kql. Only string / datetime columns
// are read below, so the LocationDetails type split documented there does
// not apply and a plain union is enough.
union SigninLogs, AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where ClientAppUsed in~ (LegacyClients)
// Future-proof equivalent (catches new legacy labels automatically):
// | where isnotempty(ClientAppUsed)
//       and ClientAppUsed !in~ ("Browser", "Mobile Apps and Desktop clients")
| summarize Attempts  = count(),
            Successes = countif(ResultType == "0"),
            Users     = make_set(UserPrincipalName, 50),
            IPs       = make_set(IPAddress, 50),
            Clients   = make_set(ClientAppUsed, 20),
            Apps      = make_set(AppDisplayName, 20)
        by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| extend StillSucceeding = Successes > 0
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
